ation being kind of short it's  not that short but i thought it was just  like a little bit shorter than maybe it  should have been but after i read to the  end i was just kind of like oh okay i  kind of feel i kind of felt like i knew  why he maybe did that at that point so  it didn't like bother me as much so all  in all uh i would definitely recommend  this if you're a fan of like movies like  the exorcist or rosemary's baby or  amityville horror which i mentioned  before  it's a very very classic demon  possession style narrative but  it has kind of enough unique character  to make it its own thing and make it  worthwhile and it comes across as like  real gruesome like a bunch of real gory  [ __ ] happens in it and it's very very  cinematic like the way that it's written  uh so that was definitely like points in  its favor you know it moved along at a  good pace and it introduced um i think  my favorite concept about it was the  demon being able to like show you really  realistic hallucinations so you were  never really sure if what the  protagonists were seeing was what was  really going on because they would each  see their own thing like and it was like  i said tailored specifically to them  like because the demon knew what would  bother them the most and so it would  show them that like other people would  be like what the [ __ ] are you looking at  i don't see anything so it was that kind  of thing so i really liked that there  was that kind of ambiguity about  what you were seeing and like whether it  was real or not so i thought that was  like kind of cool and i think that was  probably like my best part of the story  and honestly i kind of feel like this  would be a really good one you know now  that it's september at last so we're  coming up into fall and we're coming up  into halloween and everything like that  and this seemed to me even though it's  actually set in the spring and summer  it actually comes across to me as like  just kind of like a real